  data: {
    LLM: 'Prioritize captures that win clubs and key scoring cards (2 of Clubs, 10 of Diamonds). Avoid leaving easy 11-combinations for opponents.\n\nManage tableau totals: leaving 10 or less often invites an opponent sur. Use face cards to break arithmetic capture patterns when you cannot profitably capture.\n\nTrack club majority race and sur state simultaneously. In two-player games, preserving jack timing can force opponent exposure and improve end-control for last-capture advantage.',
    Player: 'Prioritize captures that win clubs and key scoring cards (2 of Clubs, 10 of Diamonds). Avoid leaving easy 11-combinations for opponents.\n\nManage tableau totals: leaving 10 or less often invites an opponent sur. Use face cards to break arithmetic capture patterns when you cannot profitably capture.\n\nTrack club majority race and sur state simultaneously. In two-player games, preserving jack timing can force opponent exposure and improve end-control for last-capture advantage.',
